From 6726c1b81185c1124f836a00abe1954fffafe8bd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 06:21:57 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(slice): section touching or stacked solids as their union

A soup that meets a slice plane 3+ ways is retried as the union of its
closed solids: facets are split into bodies by shared-edge connectivity
(corners welded within 0.1 um), and only when every body is a closed,
consistently wound 2-manifold with positive volume is each body sliced
alone and the sections united. Anything else - solids welded along a
shared edge or face, an open body, an inward cavity shell - keeps the
non-manifold refusal, now worded as the model's fault with the fix.
Meshes that sliced before never reach the fallback.

The generators map Open/NonManifold slice faults to a new
GenError::Model ("the source model cannot be sliced: ...") instead of
"invalid machining parameters".

The touching-bodies section readers (material_above_of,
material_overhead_of) move to slice_bodies with the fallback, re-exported
from slice (400-line law).

Fixes #1407

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
